 "title": "Ion trap quantum computation",
 "short": "Ion trap quantum computation",
 "lead": "How trapped ions become a quantum computer: two ions in one trap share their motion through the Coulomb repulsion, which splits into a <span data-concept=\"ion-normal-modes\">center-of-mass mode and a stretch mode</span>; the internal levels serve as <span data-concept=\"qubit\">qubits</span>, and the shared motion carries the interaction a two-qubit <span data-concept=\"pi-phase-gate\">phase gate</span> needs.",
