  {
   "id": "two-ion-hamiltonian",
   "what": "the Hamiltonian of two trapped ions in the laser light",
   "source": "Modern Atomic and Optical Physics II, 10.4 Ion trap quantum computation, 10.4.1",
   "nodes": [
    {
     "assumes": [
      {
       "tex": "\\hat{x} = \\sqrt{\\frac{\\hbar}{2\\km\\knu}}\\left(\\hat{a} + \\hat{a}^\\dagger\\right)",
       "src": "(10.2)"
      },
      {
       "tex": "{\\kH_{motion}} = {\\left(\\frac{\\kPcm^2}{2\\km} + \\frac{\\km}{2}\\knu^2 \\kXcm^2\\right)} + {\\left(\\frac{\\kpcm^2}{2\\km} + \\frac{\\km}{2}3\\knu^2 \\kxdisp^2\\right)}",
       "src": "(10.37)"
      }
     ],
     "then": {
      "tex": "\\mk{L}{\\kkmag\\kxdisp_{1,2}} = \\mk{R}{\\frac{\\kkmag}{\\sqrt{2}}(\\kXcm \\mp \\kxdisp)}",
      "src": "(10.33), (10.34)",
      "uses": [],
      "why": "Adding and subtracting (10.33) and (10.34) gives $x_1$ and $x_2$."
     },
     "steps": [
      {
       "tex": "\\mk{L}{\\kkmag\\kxdisp_{1,2}} = \\mk{R}{\\frac{\\kkmag}{\\sqrt{2}}\\left(\\sqrt{\\frac{\\hbar}{2\\km\\knu}}(\\hat{a}_{cm}+\\hat{a}_{cm}^\\dagger) \\mp \\sqrt{\\frac{\\hbar}{2\\km\\knus}}(\\hat{a}_{s}+\\hat{a}_{s}^\\dagger)\\right)}",
       "uses": [
        0,
        1
       ],
       "cap": "Each bracket of (10.37) is an oscillator of mass $m$, the center-of-mass mode at $\\nu$ and the stretch mode at $\\sqrt{3}\\nu$, so (10.2) holds for each at its own frequency."
      },
      {
       "tex": "\\mk{L}{\\kkmag\\kxdisp_{1,2}} = \\mk{R}{\\eta_{cm}(\\hat{a}_{cm}+\\hat{a}_{cm}^\\dagger) \\mp \\eta_s(\\hat{a}_{s}+\\hat{a}_{s}^\\dagger)}",
       "uses": [],
       "cap": "Writing $\\eta_{cm} = k\\sqrt{\\hbar/4m\\nu}$ and $\\eta_s = k\\sqrt{\\hbar/4m\\sqrt{3}\\nu}$, the Lamb-Dicke parameters of the two modes."
      }
     ],
     "note": "The book uses $\\eta_{cm}$ and $\\eta_s$ in (10.39) without defining them. In terms of the single-ion parameter $\\ketaLD = \\kkmag\\kazero$ of (10.12), $\\eta_{cm} = \\ketaLD/\\sqrt{2}$ and $\\eta_s = \\ketaLD/(\\sqrt{2}\\cdot 3^{1/4}) \\approx 0.54\\,\\ketaLD$."
    },
    {
     "assumes": [
      {
       "step": 0
      },
      {
       "tex": "{\\kH_{motion}} = {\\left(\\frac{\\kPcm^2}{2\\km} + \\frac{\\km}{2}\\knu^2 \\kXcm^2\\right)} + {\\left(\\frac{\\kpcm^2}{2\\km} + \\frac{\\km}{2}3\\knu^2 \\kxdisp^2\\right)}",
       "src": "(10.37)"
      },
      {
       "tex": "\\kH_\\mathrm{motion} = \\hbar\\knu\\hat{a}^\\dagger\\hat{a}",
       "src": "(10.4)"
      },
      {
       "tex": "\\kH_{int} = -\\sum_i\\left(\\hbar\\kDelta_i|e\\rangle_{ii}\\langle e| + \\hbar\\kOmega_i\\left(|e\\rangle_{ii}\\langle g|e^{i\\kkmag \\kxdisp_i} + h.c.\\right)\\right)",
       "src": "(10.38)"
      }
     ],
     "then": {
      "tex": "\\mk{H}{\\kH} = \\mk{M}{\\kH_{motion}} + \\mk{I}{\\kH_{int}}",
      "src": "10.4.1",
      "uses": [],
      "why": "The full Hamiltonian is the motion of the two ions and their coupling to the light."
     },
     "steps": [
      {
       "tex": "\\mk{H}{\\kH} = \\mk{M}{\\hbar\\knu\\hat{a}_{cm}^\\dagger\\hat{a}_{cm} + \\hbar\\knus\\hat{a}_s^\\dagger\\hat{a}_s} + \\mk{I}{\\kH_{int}}",
       "uses": [
